# Network Overview

## Purpose
This document outlines the network architecture of the home lab environment, including segmentation, routing, and infrastructure components.

---

## Architecture

Internet → ISP Gateway → pfSense → Switch → Lab Devices

---

## Network Segments

### WAN (External Network)
- Source: ISP Gateway
- IP Range: Private (DHCP assigned)
- pfSense WAN IP: DHCP (private range)

---

### LAN (Internal Lab Network)
- Network: 192.168.50.0/24
- Gateway: 192.168.50.1
- DHCP Range: 192.168.50.10 – 192.168.50.100

---

## Core Components

- pfSense Firewall (routing, NAT, DHCP)
- Managed Switch (segmentation, distribution)
- Patch Panel (structured cabling)

---

## Traffic Flow

Devices → pfSense → ISP Gateway → Internet

---

## Security Model

- Segmented internal network
- Firewall enforcement at pfSense
- Isolation between lab and home network

---

## Future Improvements

- VLAN segmentation
- IDS/IPS (Snort / Suricata)
- VPN access
- Zero Trust architecture

---

## Notes

- Lab operates behind ISP router (double NAT)
- Designed for experimentation and security testing
